><surname>Klonoff</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hickman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Kashima</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Parekh</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>15</volume><issue>1</issue><year>2005</year><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><article-title>Cigarette advertising in black, Latino, and white magazines, 1998-2002: an exploratory investigation</article-title><source>Ethn Dis</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15720050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>Emotions are not 'Kooling' down in tobacco wars</source><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><publisher-name>Black Press USA</publisher-name><month>11</month><day>28</day><year>2004</year><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://news.newamericamedia.org/news/view_article.html?article_id=ea97a9324f18d19452eac647a8825d53">http://news.newamericamedia.org/news/view_article.html?article_id=ea97a9324f18d19452eac647a8825d53</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="web"><source>Office of the Attorney General of New York State. R.J. Reynolds agrees to significant restrictions on future promotions. Press release</source><month>10</month><day>6</day><year>2004</year><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.oag.state.ny.us/press/2004/oct/oct6c_04.html">http://www.oag.state.ny.us/press/2004/oct/oct6c_04.html</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>Tobacco situation and outlook yearbook. Tables 1 and 5</source><publisher-loc>Washington (DC)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>U.S. Department of Agriculture, Economic Research Servic